Package: pswmap
Title: Propensity-Score-Weighted Meta-Analytic Predictive Priors with Missing External Covariates
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Wentao", "Guo", email = "Wentao.Guo@colostate.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person(c("Angela", "Y."), "Zhu", email = "angela.zhu@boehringer-ingelheim.com", role = "aut"))
Description: Borrows external control data (for example historical trials or real-world data) for the control arm of
    a randomized trial through a propensity-score-weighted meta-analytic predictive (PSW-MAP) prior. A propensity
    score is estimated separately for each external source, each source is summarized by its odds-weighted (Hajek)
    mean and design-based variance, and the summaries are combined in a robust meta-analytic predictive prior.
    Baseline covariates that are missing in the external data are handled by complete-case weighting, by native
    missing-data handling of the propensity score learner, or by multiple imputation within each source combined by
    Rubin's rules. An analysis of the trial alone is available as a reference. Continuous outcomes are supported.
